# avogadrodata is a fixture repository: the test suite compares against these
# files byte for byte, so every one of them has to arrive exactly as committed.
#
# Git's end-of-line conversion breaks that. On a Windows checkout it rewrites
# the text fixtures to CRLF while leaving the compressed ones alone, because
# those are binary -- so data/xyz/methane.xyz arrived with CRLF while
# data/compressed/methane.xyz.gz still decompressed to the LF bytes it was
# built from, and eight compression tests failed on the mismatch. Turning off
# the conversion keeps every fixture byte-identical on every platform.
* -text
